# Felothar's sacrifice is a choice made as the trigger resolves (CR 701.21a, 603.12): declining it on entering puts no counters
# on anything. On turn 3 it attacks and Bot1 sacrifices Felothar itself, a nonland permanent: the reflexive ability still
# resolves and puts a counter on the Ornithopter, the one creature left, though Felothar deals no damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose()
? Bot1.Battlefield.Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan.Power = 3
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Felothar, Dawn of the Abzan
Bot2.Life = 20
